sxml serialize - Write an XML document by a serialization method

Usage: sxml serialize [--indent] [--method=METHOD] FILE

Parses FILE as namespace-well-formed XML 1.0 and writes the document
to standard output by the Serialization 4.0 method --method names
(xml by default) with its default parameters; --indent indents. A
FILE that is not well-formed is reported as FILE:LINE:COLUMN: message
and exits 1; an unreadable file exits 3.

Options:
  -h, --help           Show this help and exit
      --indent         Indent the output
      --method=METHOD  Serialization method (one of: adaptive, xml, xhtml, html, text, json; default: xml)

Arguments:
  FILE  XML document to write; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml serialize --indent book.xml
  sxml serialize --method=html page.xml
